holtrace-prune: Store trace records in compact arrays

The upstream pruner retains a Python tuple for each trace record and a
Python list slot for every input line. Large proof traces can exhaust
the memory of the runner before pruning completes. Store record fields
and ID maps in packed arrays, and store tags and marks as bytes.

The traversal and output order remain unchanged. The compact storage
rejects invalid fields and references to IDs that have not been mapped.
The pruner is outside the trusted base: replay and accepted-file
comparison still check the resulting trace.

